## Summary

Extract the pre-existing test race discussed in [#85776](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/pull/85776#discussion_r4149974359) into a separate fix against `main`.

`TestUpdateLogLevelAppliesToNextWindowLogMessagesAsync` collects `window/logMessage` callbacks in a mutable `List<string>` and reads it after disposing the server. The real shutdown callback can still insert a message after disposal returns, including during assertion enumeration.

Use `ConcurrentQueue<string>` and take one `ToArray()` snapshot for the four existing membership assertions. The queue retains enqueue order for debugging, unlike a concurrent bag. No product behavior, callback scheduling, xUnit imports, or completion-source options change.

## Controlled reproduction on main

Base: `d95fce4d81f2809e06449b1413752764ccc2bd45` (xUnit v2).

A temporary test used the actual `CreateLanguageServerAsync` server and its `LogMessageReceived` event, not a fabricated background producer:

1. Block the real `Shutting down` notification callback immediately before adding its message to the collection.
2. Await `server.DisposeAsync()`. It completes while that callback is still blocked.
3. Obtain the collection enumerator, then release the callback and await its insertion.
4. Advance the enumerator.

With the original `List<string>`, this fails with:

```text
Server disposal completed while the shutdown log callback was blocked before List.Add.
Shutdown callback mutated the collection after disposal and after enumeration began.
System.InvalidOperationException: Collection was modified; enumeration operation may not execute.
   at System.Collections.Generic.List`1.Enumerator.MoveNext()
```

With the queue and a snapshot obtained at the same point, the controlled interleaving passes. This proves a permitted failing interleaving on main; it does not establish the origin of the earlier Linux CI failure. The installed StreamJsonRpc 2.26.114 also documents that local methods may outlive disposal/`Completion` and that `DispatchCompletion` is the separate dispatch-draining primitive. The current client harness does not await that primitive. xUnit v2's collection membership assertions enumerate the collection.

<details>
<summary>Temporary failing probe (add to ServerInitializationTests to reproduce on the base commit)</summary>

```csharp
[Fact]
public async Task TestShutdownLogCollectionRaceReproAsync()
{
    var logMessages = new List<string>();
    var callbackEntered = new TaskCompletionSource(TaskCreationOptions.RunContinuationsAsynchronously);
    var callbackCompleted = new TaskCompletionSource(TaskCreationOptions.RunContinuationsAsynchronously);
    using var releaseCallback = new ManualResetEventSlim();
    var server = await CreateLanguageServerAsync();
    Task? disposal = null;
    server.LogMessageReceived += logMessage =>
    {
        if (logMessage.Message.Contains("Shutting down", StringComparison.Ordinal))
        {
            callbackEntered.TrySetResult();
            if (!releaseCallback.Wait(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30)))
            {
                callbackCompleted.TrySetException(new TimeoutException("Shutdown callback was not released."));
                return;
            }

            logMessages.Add(logMessage.Message);
            callbackCompleted.TrySetResult();
        }
    };

    try
    {
        disposal = server.DisposeAsync().AsTask();
        await callbackEntered.Task.WaitAsync(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30));
        await disposal.WaitAsync(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30));
        TestOutputHelper.WriteLine("Server disposal completed while the shutdown log callback was blocked before List.Add.");

        using var enumerator = logMessages.GetEnumerator();
        releaseCallback.Set();
        await callbackCompleted.Task.WaitAsync(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30));
        TestOutputHelper.WriteLine("Shutdown callback mutated the collection after disposal and after enumeration began.");
        Assert.False(enumerator.MoveNext());
    }
    finally
    {
        releaseCallback.Set();
        if (disposal is not null)
        {
            await disposal.WaitAsync(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30));
        }

        await callbackCompleted.Task.WaitAsync(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30));
    }
}
```

For the passing variant, use `ConcurrentQueue<string>`/`Enqueue` and obtain the enumerator from the `ToArray()` snapshot instead. The temporary probe was removed from the product diff; this description preserves it for reproduction.

</details>

