Fixes #53621

### Summary
Adds overloads for `IOperation.Descendants` and `IOperation.DescendantsAndSelf` accepting an optional `Func<IOperation, bool>? descendIntoChildren` predicate, as approved in API review (#53621).

### API Changes
```csharp
namespace Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Operations
{
    public static class OperationExtensions
    {
        public static IEnumerable<IOperation> Descendants(this IOperation? operation, Func<IOperation, bool>? descendIntoChildren);
        public static IEnumerable<IOperation> DescendantsAndSelf(this IOperation? operation, Func<IOperation, bool>? descendIntoChildren);
    }
}
```

### Details
- Updates internal `OperationExtensions.Descendants` traversal to check `descendIntoChildren(operation)` on the root (yielding the root if `includeSelf: true`, but pruning child traversal if `false`), and `descendIntoChildren(current)` before pushing children of traversed operations.
- Preserves existing behavior when `descendIntoChildren` is null (the parameterless overloads forward `descendIntoChildren: null`).
- Registers public symbols in `src/Compilers/Core/Portable/PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt`.
- Adds unit tests in `OperationTests.cs` verifying null operation handling, null predicate equivalence, lambda/local function pruning, and root pruning semantics.

